587	// Filter one edge's crossing findings through its reviewed exceptions. Returns
588	// the survivors plus the stale (path, to) pairs — exceptions that matched no
589	// crossing, meaning the coupling they excused is gone and the entry should be
590	// pruned. A `to`-less exception excuses every crossing from its file; a pinned
591	// one only crossings landing under a named barred folder, per to-entry.
