7	// rule to its file, how a pack's carriers are enumerated and which file each one
8	// names, and the two codemods that put a pack onto the convention (`markPack`,
9	// `convertReferences`). Every reader and writer of a `provenance/` folder composes
10	// this — the growth pack's checks and CLI, the migration-registry op that marks a
11	// member's local packs at converge — so the grammar is spelled once, here, and
12	// nothing below carries a rule's failure text or a command's wording (those are the
13	// callers'). The convention itself — what an element is, what an entry records, what
14	// is never vendored — is docs/provenance/DESIGN.md's; this module is what it says a
15	// file looks like.
16	//
17	// io is injected everywhere — `{ read, write, exists, listDir, remove? }` over
18	// repo-relative posix paths — so the same code runs over a checkout (the CLI) and
19	// inside the registry's record io (a member's converge) without a second
20	// implementation.
