    Judge a push overtaken on the base branch against its own before (#2175)

    * Judge a push overtaken on the base branch against its own before

    The CI work-scope step decided "this is a push onto the base branch" by
    HEAD equalling the freshly fetched origin/main. On a busy trunk the base
    takes further merges and a version bump in the minute between a push and
    its step, so HEAD is an ancestor of the base rather than equal to it, the
    push-event path is never taken, and the three-dot diff from a base that
    already holds HEAD is empty, which the step refuses and fails the run.
    Containment is the test now, so an overtaken push is judged against the
    event's `before` like any other.

